e) that throughput is capped to ~0.9-1.3 Mbit/s","Verified node1's own traffic to node3 over br-lan remains unshaped (~119 Gbit/s), after temporarily opening firewalld port 5201 on node3 for the test then closing it again","Persisted the tc shaping via /etc/hotplug.d/iface/95-shape-eth1 script triggered on ifup of the priv interface, so it reapplies after reboot","Captured pre-restart boot_id, uptime, interface state, and tc state as baseline for node1, node2, node3","Restarted node1 via 'reboot', polled until exec available again, confirmed changed boot_id, confirmed eth1 IP and tc shaping rules were automatically reapplied via hotplug script, re-verified ~1Mbit/s shaping still in effect with iperf3","Restarted node2 via 'reboot', polled until exec available again, confirmed changed boot_id, confirmed eth1 static IP persisted, re-verified ping and shaped iperf3 throughput to node1","Restarted node3 via 'reboot', polled until exec available again, confirmed changed boot_id, confirmed connectivity to node1 recovered"],"evidence":[{"requirement":"Baseline private-link discovery and unshaped throughput measurement","command_ids":["cmd-9473b2b760ad4df7","cmd-5c074f6f808840dd","cmd-1ef6fbceccc54657","cmd-c2ce9559a314478a","cmd-b67fc416300a403f"],"summary":"Identified unconfigured eth1 on node1/node2 as the private link; measured baseline unshaped throughput at ~80,000-120,000 Mbit/s"},{"requirement":"Private link configured and reachable","command_ids":["cmd-4a48eefe90eb4bdc","cmd-19ef84c80ebe4410","cmd-3eb34a2ab8074de4","cmd-3f0df62648974263"],"summary":"Static IPs assigned on eth1 (192.168.50.1/.2), firewall zone added, ping verified both directions"},{"requirement":"1Mbit/s shaping applied on node1 for node2's traffic, each direction","command_ids":["cmd-8a63effe43e145b7","cmd-5ad55a60208040fc","cmd-6ce3a1d0a0414286"],"summary":"tc tbf egress qdisc and tc ingress police filter (1mbit each) installed on node1's eth1"},{"requirement":"Demonstrate ~1Mbit/s limit with mea